From ba003783dd7ef9f3a61b12a2df30e2b3d5a5cb0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kurtvan <kurtv7348@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:08:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Let the caller find a preset's loaded image textures

Adds projectm_get_preset_texture(instance, name, &texture, &width,
&height). A preset's shaders resolve their textures once, at load, and
bind the same GL texture every frame, so a caller that draws into the
returned texture (e.g. live video) changes what the preset samples from
the next frame on, with no reload and no new GL objects in projectM.

Only already-loaded image files are returned (looked up by lower-case
name, as TextureManager stores them); the missing-texture placeholder
and the built-in noise/idle textures never are.
